## Tool Call Format

{% if native_tools %}
Call tools through the tool-calling interface. A tool call written as text, XML, or JSON in your message is not executed.
Every response must call at least one tool. Multiple tool calls in one response are executed sequentially, in order.
Do not repeat the same tool call in one response unless the user explicitly asks for repeated identical actions.
{% if parallel_tools %}
Prefer combining actions in one response when targets are visible and won't move — e.g. type into a field then tap a button on the same dialog. Use separate responses when an action may change the screen.
{% endif %}
{% else %}
To call a tool, wrap it in <function_calls> tags:

<function_calls>
<invoke name="TOOL_NAME">
<parameter name="PARAM_NAME">value</parameter>
</invoke>
</function_calls>

The <function_calls> tag always starts a tool call. Write tool-call tags only inside the call, never in your explanation.
Multiple <invoke> blocks in one <function_calls> block are executed sequentially, in order.
Emit exactly one <function_calls> block per response. If you need multiple actions, put multiple <invoke> blocks inside that single block.
Do not repeat the same tool call in one response unless the user explicitly asks for repeated identical actions.
{% if parallel_tools %}
Prefer combining actions in one block when targets are visible and won't move — e.g. type into a field then tap a button on the same dialog. Use separate calls when an action may change the screen.
{% endif %}
{% endif %}

